# Phase 9 checks for reviews (testimonials) (VS Code REST Client: click "Send Request" above a block).
# Start the API first (npm run dev:api) and load the sample data (npm run seed:api). Reviews and replies
# made here stay in the database (a reply also goes to the customer's chat): run npm run seed:api again afterwards.
#
# The customer requests need a customer token and the admin requests an admin token: get them with the
# sign-in requests at the top of catalog.http, and paste them into @customerToken and @adminToken below.
# @ref is one of that customer's completed events without a review: GET /reservations shows their bookings
# (refs follow the sample data's dates, which count from the day it was loaded). @review is a review id
# (tst-001 … tst-009 in the sample data). Errors come back as { code, message, meta }.

@api = http://localhost:4000/api
@customerToken = paste-a-customer-token
@adminToken = paste-an-admin-token
@ref = paste-a-completed-ref
@review = tst-009

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Public (no token)

### The website's reviews: published, not flagged or archived, featured first. Only id, rating, categories,
### body, featured, createdAt, customerName and eventName (no email, mobile, customer id or ref). limit 1-20, default 3
GET {{api}}/feedback/published?limit=3

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Customer

### The customer's own reviews, newest first (no flagReason, no customerMobile)
GET {{api}}/feedback
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Review a completed event -> 201 with the review (hidden until the admin publishes it, unread by the admin).
### Not their own completed event: 409 "Feedback opens once an event is completed."; reviewed already: 409;
### stars, a missing category or under 20 characters: 400 INVALID with meta.field (rating, categories, body)
POST {{api}}/feedback
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ref": "{{ref}}", "rating": 5, "categories": { "food": 5, "service": 5, "punctuality": 4, "setup": 5 }, "body": "The food was still warm at the last dance. Thank you, Tres Marias!" }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Admin

### Every review, newest first, with flagReason and customerMobile
GET {{api}}/admin/feedback
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### How many are unread (a number)
GET {{api}}/admin/feedback/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Mark one as read -> the review
POST {{api}}/admin/feedback/{{review}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Mark every review as read -> { marked }
POST {{api}}/admin/feedback/read-all
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Publish on the website or take it off: "published" | "hidden" (flagged or archived: 409; hiding also unfeatures)
PATCH {{api}}/admin/feedback/{{review}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "published" }

### Feature it (publishes it; not while flagged or archived) or { "featured": false }
PATCH {{api}}/admin/feedback/{{review}}/featured
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "featured": true }

### Flag it with a reason only the admin sees (at least 5 characters; takes it off the website), or { "flagged": false }
PATCH {{api}}/admin/feedback/{{review}}/flag
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "flagged": true, "reason": "Checking the service report for this date first." }

### Archive it (off the website) or { "archived": false } to restore it
PATCH {{api}}/admin/feedback/{{review}}/archived
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "archived": true }

### Reply (5-1,000 characters): saved under the review, signed with the admin's name, and sent to the
### customer's chat as "About your feedback on <event>: …". Replying again replaces it and sends the new one.
POST {{api}}/admin/feedback/{{review}}/reply
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Thank you for celebrating with us! We are glad the food stayed warm." }

### Delete for good -> { ok: true } (the customer may then write a new review). Again: 404
DELETE {{api}}/admin/feedback/{{review}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
